WEBVTT

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:46.870
Like, on this morning gossip show, like, they were doin' this "bust-up!" massage thing.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.250
Like this?

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.460
Yeah, like that.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.720
I see.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.740
Like this.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.630
I see.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.950
Okay!  We're gonna get us some awesome plump busts too!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.030
Good morning...

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.530
Kageyama Torako-kun.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.730
Good morning, uh... Who are you?

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.880
I am Andou Nene.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.360
You don't remember, even though we're classmates?

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.900
Right.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.080
Um, Andou-san...

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.870
That's an amazing look you have.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:23.990
Indeed.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.250
Sorry about the short notice, but did you know you're on the disciplinary committee?

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.500
The disciplinary committee?

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.880
I'm on the disciplinary committee?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.020
Just as I thought.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.740
Huh?  I had no idea!  When was this decided?

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.090
When, you say?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:46.610
During the time you were absent just after the entrance ceremony, obviously.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:51.670
All the jobs people didn't want to do were split up among the people who were conveniently absent.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.140
Oh, so that's when.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.530
Speaking of which, Saotome-kun, you're on the tree-planting committee.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.270
Tree-planting committee?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.110
You mean like that?

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:05.860
It seems you two were absent from yesterday's general committee meeting.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.500
Word has reached me, you see.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.050
Word reached you?  Who are you, exactly?

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:12.790
Me?

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.340
<i>Me</i>?

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.050
Yeah...

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.130
I...

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.220
...am the class president!

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.560
The president?!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.730
No way in hell!

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.270
An amusing reaction, Kageyama-kun.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.870
That's totally unexpected.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.730
At least wear glasses or something!

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.110
Oh, so you're one of those glasses people.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.490
No!  Don't go classifying me!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.590
Fine, whatever.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.450
Anyway, it's time I got to the main topic.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.710
Main topic?

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:54.350
About the uniform check the disciplinary committee is running starting tomorrow.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.880
A uniform check?

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:19.630
So it's called, but the actual rules regarding uniforms are practically non-existent at our school.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.650
And it's not like there's any special penalties, either.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.480
This is really all just for show.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:30.910
Well, our job is simply to give a warning to those students who seem really out there.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:31.910
Sleepy...

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:37.250
I think <i>your</i> outfit is pretty out there, personally...

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:40.380
Does the class pres have to be like this or something?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.880
No, it's optional.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.410
It's just for scoring myself some points.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.720
Scoring points?

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.250
For what?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.060
For me to become the student council president.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.800
Student coun...

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.900
You want to become the student council president too?

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.730
Indeed.  All in due time.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.440
Just for the fun of it...

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.600
And if you become that, what will you do?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:06.220
Good question!  First, I'd want to start by raising the hem of the girl's skirts by five centimeters.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.230
Whoa...

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.140
Mornin's all.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.220
Blech...

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.750
Hey, Amagasa-sensei.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.990
Whatup.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.050
Sure is tough, bright and early like this...

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.300
Anyway, I'm not gonna butt-in or anything.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.320
'cause it's a pain...

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.230
So you girls just do a couple spot checks.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.850
Just leave it to us!

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.740
Hey, no slacking, Kageyama!

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.570
'kay!

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:39.520
Jeez, spot checks or no slacking?  Which is it?

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.810
Hey, Kageyama-kun!  Take a look over there!

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:43.440
Huh?

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.130
What a crazy outfit!

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.690
Isn't that what they call "punk?"

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:54.370
"Punk?"  Yeah, like in the 80's.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.430
Kageyama-kun, go give her a warning.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:58.430
No way!

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:01.170
What'll I do if she turns and counter-attacks me with that thing she's carrying!

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.880
And why have you gone and decided that she's got something on her?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.130
Aren't you the one that just said she was a punk?

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.510
So what?

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:13.600
Are you saying she run away on a stolen bike, or walks around at night breaking all the school windows?

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.140
I didn't say anything like that!

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.640
Whatever, just go!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.480
You're on the disciplinary committee, remember?

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.690
You go!

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.110
You're the next student council president, right?

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:24.200
The next student council president isn't going to risk her life on such a trivial matter.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.290
This is a matter for someone like you to handle.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:26.770
Someone like you!

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.010
I'm not on the disciplinary committee 'cause I wanted to be!

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:29.650
You go!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:30.860
You're the one that should go!

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:31.570
You!

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.070
Fine, whatever!  We'll decided this with rock-paper-scissors.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.410
Hey you.  Wear your uniform properly!

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:41.330
Huh?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.990
What business is it of yours?  Get lost.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.800
And who the hell are you to talk anyway.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.500
See?  She didn't have anything on her!

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.120
To start, judging people based on their appearance,

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.560
or saying things like "a diamond in the rough", er, I mean "she's just rotten,"

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.550
it's this problem we have as human beings that, as the next student council president I will show that we,

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.640
like the character for "person" must support one another, we cannot live alone...

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:07.280
Sorry, I guess I should have gone...

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.190
Still, she had a pretty good point there.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.290
Hey, look.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.550
How about we have a word with that person next.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.520
Indeed.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.200
Hey, you.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.960
Huh?  Me?

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.340
About your uniform...

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.510
Are you on the disciplinary committee?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.840
Oh, shoot...

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.410
You should really be more restrained.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:36.970
Oh, that's right.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.290
Could you please overlook this?

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.230
W-What?

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.730
Pre-paid meal tickets good for one year

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.510
You may pass.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.200
Nice doin' business with ya.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.700
H-H-H-Hey!  What did you just accept?!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:57.060
You're exactly the type of person we can't have becoming the student council president!

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:01.030
This sort of thing is fundamental for being successful in this world!

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.290
She doesn't find anything wrong with it.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.930
That's it for Japan.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.890
Here comes a fresh mark.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.340
You call them "marks," now?

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.350
Hey you, over there!

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.590
W-What?

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.360
She's huge.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.150
What?  What?  What?

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.060
You pass!

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.450
I have work to do now, but we'll talk later.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.700
Quite nice today.  Excellent, indeed.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.680
What did you mean by "pass?"

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:46.250
Well, this school has quite a number of unique students.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.430
Good morning.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:02.720
Your glasses are quite bright.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.990
Oh, thanks...

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.440
Ooh, she's not bad either...

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.310
Well, there are them, too.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.290
Them?  Them, what?

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.330
Good morning, Touma!

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:30.540
I say, "Good morning, Touma!"

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.550
You say, "Good morning!"

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.210
Ooh, nice, nice.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:36.820
She's quite the tsundere.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:41.010
Note:  The otaku trope "tsundere" is a portmanteau of "tsuntsun" (aloof) and "deredere" (lovestruck).

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.580
She ain't got a "dere" bone in her body!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.010
All the more to look forward to!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.890
What's with you?

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.010
Hey, what's with her?

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.790
Why is she like that?

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.860
Isn't that Saotome-kun?

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.720
What?  What happened... to you?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.970
Where're your clothes?

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.630
It's because first period is gym class.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:26.520
"Because?"  You wouldn't even do this in elementary school.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.380
And she's not even the least bit embarrassed.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.280
Why today, of all days.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.760
At least put on a jersey or something...

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.930
And to make things worse, our school's gym uniform shouldn't be bloomers to begin with!

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:39.240
She deliberately went and bought those?

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.200
Yes, but... This is, well...

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.120
What are you talking about?

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:51.370
Um, look, see... You've been...

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.250
Good morning, Torako-san!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.840
And... Andou-san?

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:02.180
And, Suzume-san, where are your clothes?

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:04.970
Yeah, figured this'd happen.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.630
Now look here!  What in the world have you made her do!

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.770
Hey, don't make me out to be the bad guy here!

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.440
She chose to look like that herself!

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:20.240
Hey, Boss.  Give this girl here a uniform check too.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.740
Let's see here.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:25.950
What is it?

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.910
How rude.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.010
Light blue polka-dots, huh?

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.800
Nice and healthy, a winner.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.010
Hey, you've got a nosebleed.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:51.260
Um, well, Andou-san...

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.100
Do you like women?

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.470
Women?

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.100
That's not it.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:00.990
I'm bi!

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.590
Bi = Bisexual
[Noun, Adjective]
To be attracted to people of both the same and opposite sex.
Also, a person who has this characteristic.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.250
I'm bi!

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.530
And by the way, the four of you are totally my type!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.760
Too much information!

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.370
Health committee?

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.370
Looks good on you!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.370
Suzugasaki, be quiet!

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.450
What's so amusing over there?

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:57.290
But, President, I'm just so happy we've finished it.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:00.600
Oh that.  Yeah, it took a long time, didn't it?

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.650
After we install that, we'll test it out again tomorrow.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.870
For real?  All right!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.430
Robot Society

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.430
I said be quiet, Suzugasaki!

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:32.580
Enough already... The bleeding's stopped, so...

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.860
Let's go back. I'm sure Ayu and the others are waiting.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.930
I should have never let you handle it, Ta-chan.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:43.780
How could you not know where the nurse's office is?

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.340
How many years have you been going to this school?

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.040
Idiot.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.830
Zero sense of direction.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.780
A counter-attack?

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:59.020
That is right!  A counter-attack!

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:01.520
What was that about the nurse's office again?

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.610
And besides, with such a trivial injury...

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.860
Just put a little spit on it and you'll be fine!

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.820
How about <i>I</i> be the one to provide the spit?!

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:09.820
Defiant!

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.340
What's that noise?

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.280
Is it me?

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.870
A r-robot?

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:47.820
A robot?

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.380
What is that?

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:51.060
That...

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:51.810
"That?"

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:52.780
What is that?

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:56.670
Whaddya mean?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.040
What is that?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.530
I can't read it.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:01.540
It couldn't be...

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.290
I think it's just drawn on.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:12.170
Um... We're in the same class...

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.360
I'm Kageyama.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:14.430
And I am Iizuka.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.180
Note:  From Tetsujin 28 (Gigantor)

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.180
It's Shoutaro-kun!

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.020
Ayu!

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:28.350
What's the matter?  We've been waiting this whole time.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:30.420
Did you get treated?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:31.750
For the time being (toriaezu).

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.020
Triage (toriaaji).

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:39.690
It's a robot!

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.290
You notice <i>now</i>?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.000
Robot Society

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.820
I'm Suzugasaki Chie!

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.380
Please call me Chie.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:52.010
Oh, I see.  Is making robots your hobby, Chie-san?

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.010
Have some tea.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.140
Thank you very much!

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:03.760
Isn't it weird?  Me being a girl and all...

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:04.910
Not at all!

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.520
It's totally cool!  You're one of those engineer wannabes!

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.420
Uh, well...

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:16.280
I was just thinking that I'd like to work for E-lectra in the future...

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:20.200
Wow! E-lectra is like a super big company!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:26.540
E-lectra: Written horizontally, it's E, L, E, C, T, R, A.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:32.720
It stands for Electric Life Eternal Creativity Traditional Realize Authorities.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.910
One of Japan's most venerable large electronics companies.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:38.200
The brand-name is a powerhouse around the entire world.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.830
Wow, how respectable!

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.690
Huh?  My family's...

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:43.950
What do you mean, "family?"

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:48.770
Um, well, it is like my family, or like my house...

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:54.440
Or, well, you see it is my father that is currently the president,

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:58.410
and my grandfather that was, see, the founder of the company, so...

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.050
That's like, so incredible!

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:04.130
The daughter of the company president?

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.440
W-Wow!

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.960
Is that true?

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.760
It's true!  That really is the name of the president!

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:12.090
I saw him on TV before!

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:15.230
W-Will you sh-shake my hand?

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:17.890
U-Um... I am a different person, you know.

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:22.030
So she wasn't putting on an snooty character, but was a actually a real celeb?

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:22.850
I'm totally mooching off her!

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:25.460
Takki, that's amazing!

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.180
W-Wow.

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:30.140
What's this robot's name?

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:33.470
It's an independently walking (jiritsuhokou) robot, so we call it "Hoko-chan".

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:35.120
Huh?  Which one?

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.300
Can you ride it?

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.040
N-No, you can't.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:40.510
When will you be able to ride it?

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.620
This isn't the type you can ride.

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:46.290
Can it fly?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.670
No, it can't fly.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.240
What does it battle?

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:52.580
It's not really for fighting...

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:54.220
Is it for "that agency"?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.900
Chie-chan built it mostly by herself.

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:01.010
She's really incredible.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.820
It is pretty amazing.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.850
I-I-I-I'm honored!

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:11.230
Although the top half is quite slipshod comparatively.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:13.200
Even though it's for "that agency."

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:16.360
Well, it's still in development, so...

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.670
What about "that agency?"

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:18.670
Quiet, you.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:23.080
Oh, there are many others that the more senior people in the club built.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:26.910
This is a robotic arm, to put it simply.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:31.440
And this one was experimenting with doing human communication, for a change.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:37.040
It only has 10 different patterns to respond to people and is just a simple program.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.820
Well, it was just an experiment, so...

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:43.420
Next, I think this one is kind of interesting, it really fascinates me.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:45.210
Um... Hey.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:49.470
Can I try making a robot, too?

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:15.920
I'm taking attendance.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:16.690
Akiyama.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:17.510
Here.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:18.120
Arita.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:18.860
Here.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:19.620
Andou.

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:20.510
Here!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.690
Iizuka.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:22.480
Here.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:23.430
Utagawa.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.220
Here.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.160
Oba.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:26.010
Here.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:26.910
Oki.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:27.780
Here.

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:29.310
Kageyama.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.250
Huh?  Absent?

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:33.850
Here.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.860
What was that synthetic sound?

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.340
Kageyama!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.190
Here.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.780
What the hell is this?

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.540
Kageyama, what's this?

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:02.800
No, I do not comprehend.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.530
What the heck?

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:09.920
Nonomura.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.690
Where the hell is Kageyama?

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:16.610
Why me?

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:19.420
She's right there!

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:23.830
Kageyama!

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:26.610
Hey, did you just say something?

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.550
Huh?  Say what?

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:31.830
I presume you are the one that made this, Suzugasaki.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.590
Um, well about that...

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:38.600
It's just made out of spare parts, and the idea was Kageyama-san's,

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:42.340
but I guess I was the one who put it all together!

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:44.560
Get it outta my face, now!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.500
Why are you proud of this!?

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:49.100
W-What have you done to Mecha-Torako?!

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:03.860
You want some?

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.080
It's going like "wryy, wryy"...

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.410
Kageyama!

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:24.880
Here!

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:27.550
Seems like you're here today.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:29.240
Kazamatsuri.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:29.930
Here!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:30.700
Kudou.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:31.400
Here.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:32.810
Kobayashi.

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:33.550
Here.

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:34.390
Saotome.

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:37.050
He-re.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:47.530
You goddamn brats!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.850
On Standby

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:45.310
Atmospheric Entry

00:23:20.810 --> 00:23:22.280
So, what's on Hyakko next week?

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:25.120
"Drink like a cow, eat like a horse, eat like a tiger."  It means to eat a whole lot, right?

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.040
So it's a story about the cafeteria?

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:28.300
That's right.  Tigers can eat a lot too, you know.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:29.900
And they say that "Tigers hang out with tigers."

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:30.840
It's a double feature next time too.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:31.880
And I'll finally show up!

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:34.540
Good luck.  Look forward to next time too!
